**Reasoning:** A bishop always stays on squares of the same color (parity of `row + col`). If source and target have different colors, it's unreachable (-1). If they're on the same diagonal (`|dr| == |dc|`), it takes 1 move. Otherwise, any same-colored square on an 8×8 board is reachable in exactly 2 moves (an intermediate square exists at the intersection of a diagonal from each).

```python
class Solution:
    def minBishopMoves(self, source: list[int], target: list[int]) -> int:
        sr, sc = source
        tr, tc = target
        # A bishop always stays on squares of the same color.
        # Color is determined by the parity of (row + col).
        if (sr + sc) % 2 != (tr + tc) % 2:
            return -1
        # Same diagonal: |dr| == |dc|
        if abs(sr - tr) == abs(sc - tc):
            return 1
        # Any same-colored, non-diagonal square is reachable in exactly 2 moves.
        return 2
```
